#### Pseudocode for Passed Test Cases

**1. test_initialize_game_board**
```pseudocode
CLASS Cell:
    FUNCTION __init__(is_target, is_wall):
        SET self.is_target = is_target
        SET self.is_wall = is_wall
        
CLASS Board:
    FUNCTION __init__(width, height):
        FOR y FROM 0 TO height:
            FOR x FROM 0 TO width:
                CREATE Cell() INSTANCE
        SET self.grid = 2D ARRAY OF Cells

FUNCTION test_initialize_game_board():
    CREATE Game INSTANCE
    VERIFY game.board IS NOT NULL
    VERIFY LENGTH OF game.board.grid EQUALS 10
    VERIFY LENGTH OF game.board.grid[0] EQUALS 10
```

**2. test_load_level_from_file**
```pseudocode
CLASS Game:
    FUNCTION load_state():
        IF file 'game_state.txt' EXISTS:
            OPEN file AS FILE:
                READ each line into data
                SPLIT player_data BY ','
                SET self.player.position TO new Position(x, y)
                SPLIT box_data BY '; '
                FOR each box_pos IN box_data:
                    SPLIT box_pos BY ','
                    CREATE Box(Position(x, y)) INSTANCE
                SET self.boxes TO NEW list OF Boxes

FUNCTION test_load_level_from_file():
    CALL game.load_state()
    VERIFY player.position.x EQUALS 1
    VERIFY player.position.y EQUALS 1
    VERIFY LENGTH OF game.boxes EQUALS 2
```

**3. test_move_player**
```pseudocode
CLASS Player:
    FUNCTION __init__(position):
        SET self.position = position

    FUNCTION move(direction):
        IF direction EQUALS 'up':
            DECREMENT self.position.y
        ELSE IF direction EQUALS 'down':
            INCREMENT self.position.y
        ELSE IF direction EQUALS 'left':
            DECREMENT self.position.x
        ELSE IF direction EQUALS 'right':
            INCREMENT self.position.x

FUNCTION test_move_player():
    SET initial_position = game.player.position.x
    CALL game.player.move('right')
    VERIFY game.player.position.x EQUALS initial_position + 1
```

**4. test_push_box**
```pseudocode
CLASS Box:
    FUNCTION __init__(position):
        SET self.position = position

    FUNCTION move(direction):
        IF direction EQUALS 'up':
            DECREMENT self.position.y
        ELSE IF direction EQUALS 'down':
            INCREMENT self.position.y
        ELSE IF direction EQUALS 'left':
            DECREMENT self.position.x
        ELSE IF direction EQUALS 'right':
            INCREMENT self.position.x

FUNCTION test_push_box():
    SET game.player.position TO Position(2, 2)
    SET initial_box_position = game.boxes[0].position.x
    CALL game.player.move('right')
    CALL game.boxes[0].move('right')
    VERIFY game.boxes[0].position.x EQUALS initial_box_position + 1
```

